    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters June 1st with a focus on high-upside speed and favorable sequencing. The clear headline today is **James Wood**, who paces our lineup with a 73.32 efficiency score. **James Wood** benefits from a high-leverage leadoff spot against the middling 4.41 xERA of Alcantara and maintains a projectable xwOBA of .408, making him the cornerstone for our SB and run production targets. Following closely, **Corbin Carroll** (61.26) provides the necessary velocity to exploit the base paths despite a tough matchup against Sheehan; his ability to force defensive pressure remains our primary counter to the SP\u2019s 3.21 xERA. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a vital start at 56.70, largely driven by a significant +14% platoon edge against Richardson, which keeps him firmly ahead of our marginal bench options.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the morning concerned **Kyle Karros**, whose 38.93 score fell just shy of our 40.0 floor. While **Kyle Karros** holds potential, he is hampered by a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a projected matchup against a high-efficiency defensive catcher who limits stolen base opportunities. Consequently, he remains on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more optimal matchups. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**; while both are cleared to start, their scores are suppressed by the skill of their opposing starters. We are prioritizing the higher ceiling of **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** today to ensure our scarcity-weighted categories\u2014specifically SB\u2014are protected against the risk of low-scoring, grind-out contests against the likes of Sheehan.",
